== Unconditional Johnson-radius query regimes and QROM accounting

Earlier IOPP deployments parameterized WHIR queries under conjectural proximity gaps up to capacity $1 - rho$. In 2025–2026, Crites and Stewart [CS25] disproved both correlated agreement and WHIR mutual correlated agreement at capacity $1 - rho$, and Krachun, Kazanin, and Haböck [KKH26] constructed explicit prime-field multiplicative subgroup counterexamples where proximity gaps fail arbitrarily close to capacity $1 - rho - eta$. Consequently, QSAG purges all capacity-conjecture schedules: deserializing retired wire tags `0, 1, 3` fails closed in `WhirSecurityRegime::from_u8`, and every one of the six remaining regimes sets its queries from the Johnson radius $1 - sqrt(rho_i) - eta_i$ (@regimes). They differ in how many oracle queries their accounting tolerates.

